ge the 5.6 grammar.","failure_consequence":"Time strings in the payload and reports cannot be parsed or produced byte-identically.","id":"rfc3339","redistribution":"IETF Trust (BCP 78, TLP 4.e): unmodified copies may be redistributed. Not distributed with the verifier or the spec; retrieved by reference (digest above).","retrieval":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt fetched 2026-10-19T23:30:38Z; errata status from https://www.rfc-editor.org/api/v1/errata.json fetched 2026-10-19T23:30:47Z","sections":["5.6 internet date/time format"],"title":"RFC 3339: Date and time on the Internet: timestamps"},{"digest_sha256":"6c32963b76808ec4e5f1282b5e13c5216df4670d21e1590bf29af4066f49b355","edition":"RFC 4034 (immutable RFC text)","errata":"Errata at fetch time: Held for Document Update 1, Rejected 1, Verified 4. Verified 4552 (Appendix B: carries retained, then folded) is ADOPTED: the Appendix B reference code governs, as it already folds the carry. Verified 1062 (6.2 item 3 list) is superseded by RFC 6840 section 5.1, which changes only NSEC (not a V1 type); RRSIG signer names stay lowercased. 3045 and 193 do not affect V1.","failure_consequence":"DNSKEY/RRSIG/DS cannot be parsed or canonicalized; no DNSSEC chain validates.","id":"rfc4034","redistribution":"IETF Trust (BCP 78, TLP 4.e): unmodified copies may be redistributed. Not distributed with the verifier or the spec; retrieved by reference (digest above).","retrieval":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4034.txt fetched 2026-10-19T23:30:39Z; errata status from https://www.rfc-editor.org/api/v1/errata.json fetched 2026-10-19T23:30:47Z","sections":["2 DNSKEY RDATA","3 RRSIG RDATA","5 DS RDATA","6 canonical form and order","Appendix B key tag"],"title":"RFC 4034: Resource records for the DNS security extensions"},{"digest_sha256":"8978b120636c69b2080b12768266ec48cd4c0879583310863a62f7c409908084","edition":"RFC 4035 (immutable RFC text)","errata":"Errata at fetch time: Held for Document Update 1, Rejected 1, Verified 