formal/freeze-v1/objects/spec.bin:2799:| 37 | "**Chain-order pre-commitment** (…): the git assertion's selected anchor height plus 5 is lower than the receipt's selected anchor height" (C4, claim cell) | A9:143 (C4) | Added after it: "The release that first lists the receipt's service-key entry is OpenTimestamps-stamped over its trust-configuration SHA-256, and its selected anchor height plus 5 is lower than the receipt's selected anchor height; otherwise the listing subchecks of A10.4.1 apply (`LISTING_PROOF_MISSING`, `OTS_FORMAT`, `LISTING_STAMP_MISMATCH`, `OTS_MERKLE_MISMATCH`, `HEADERS_MISSING` or `ANCHOR_PENDING_ONLY`, `OTS_TX_SHAPE`, `LISTING_NOT_PRECOMMITTED`), in the order registered there." Non-claim added: "The retrospective protection requires a conforming verifier and independently authenticated Bitcoin history for both selected anchors and their six-header segments. The receipt, listing, snapshot and git proofs must use the same independently authenticated history. For this theft protection, a signature under the possibly stolen release key is not sufficient pin authentication. Compare every used pin with independently validated Bitcoin history, or with a previously retained, independently authenticated genuine release that covers that height. An earlier release with no pin at the height supplies no witness. A party unable to establish this history has not established the retrospective protection. Authenticating only the bootstrap public-key fingerprint does not distinguish a fork signed with the stolen genuine key. An independently retained genuine release/configuration commitment can distinguish such a fork to the extent of its recorded contents and ancestry." (A10.4.1, OWNER DECISION 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) Option (e) only. **AUTHOR ADOPTED 2026-10-18** (with option (e); owner decision 2026-10-18, narrowed after review r4) | BROADEN | B |

